  "note": "Durable, tracked preservation of one bounded ZTH supervised-capability-loop dogfood rerun of the reviewed_v1 multi-source-reconciliation task. The rerun corrected the local-teacher request policy (set ICM_QWEN3_8_27B_REQUEST_POLICY=routine) that was omitted in the comparable run, and observed the routing tiers: the 1.7B worker failed the exact-match baseline (phantom filename prefix groups, 5/3 vs 24/8), the correctly-configured 27B local teacher produced a parseable intervention (teacher_parse_status:passed, failure_classification:model_capability_insufficient, candidate_prompt_patch:null) and embedded its computed answer as corrected_reference_output, and the 1.7B worker echoed that reference on rerun (byte-identical to corrected_reference_output) so the terminal disposition was ready_for_review with successful_intervention_source:local_teacher. The originally frozen fixture and its raw worker prompt were lost (cleaned /tmp, never committed); the frozen SHA 3f262c29 is unreproducible byte-exactly, so the fixture was task-identically reconstructed under a new SHA (c1197915) per Option A, not prompt-tuned; the raw rerun outputs are therefore not byte-identical to the lost original run. The genuine 1.7B counting/grounding failure is preserved (first_attempt_pass:false in both runs). See README.md and genuine_raw_evidence/NOTE.md.",
